<title>USA: U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 1,215.3 million lbs of vegoils in September in edible product output versus a revised 1,269.7 million lbs in August and 1,244.5 in September 1995.</p>
<p>U.S. factory vegoil use with refining losses were as follows:</p>
<p>   (Mln Lbs) --   Sept 96   Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p>    Soybean Oil  1,088.3   1,153.1-R   1,079.5</p>
<p> Cottonseed Oil	N/A	N/A	    N/A</p>
<p>Year-to-date oil use with refining losses (Mln Lbs):</p>
<p>				    1996	   1995</p>
<p>		 Soybean Oil   9,360.1	9,487.1</p>
<p>	    Cottonseed Oil	 N/A	    N/A</p>
<p> OUTPUT -- Soybean Crude  11,140.9     11,540.8</p>
<p>		     Refined   9,070.9	9,172.6</p>
<p>	  Cottonseed Crude     987.6	    N/A</p>
<p>		     Refined     647.8	  733.9</p>
<p>		  Corn Crude   1,558.3	1,693.0</p>
<p>		     Refined     716.6	  826.7</p>
</text>
